+# Block decoder implementation handoff
+
+This packet authors a pure input decoder and its tests. It records no executed
+scientific operation, integrated return, native conformance result, or increased
+completion count. Root owns scientific/import/test execution in the selected
+20 GiB RAM / 4 GiB scratch / zero-swap lifecycle without a wall-time budget.
+
+## Owned implementation
+
+- `gene_annotation_episode/hmmer_alignment_input_blocks.py`
+- `tests/test_hmmer_alignment_input_blocks.py`
+- This verification directory only.
+
+Public port:
+`decode_native_block_alignment(content: bytes, *, declared_format: str, alphabet: str) -> dict`.
+The dictionary is exactly packet 534 DecoderBatch with packet 536's frozen
+seven-field diagnostic and three-field details object. Formats are exactly
+`psiblast`, `selex`, `clustal`, and `clustallike`; actual explicit alphabet is
+mandatory. The shared `hmmer_alignment_input_types.py` iterator/factory are
+imported unchanged. No other application module is imported.
+
+The PSI-BLAST, SELEX and Clustal methods have distinct native state machines.
+Clustal-like uses the same native Clustal state machine with its documented
+header switch. These are whole-file formats: malformed suffixes keep the one
+record partial/invalid and never produce a successful first MSA. Default native
+weights remain missing annotation facts for root's existing calculator.
+
+The module retains source Events and sequence Segments with byte and physical
+column coordinates, positional row occurrences including duplicate names,
+SELEX native gap expansion, native RF/MM/CS/SS/SA tags, and PSI case-derived RF.
+Clustal consensus remains a consensus Event and never becomes RF. Missing and
+unknown geometry is not filled. Input NUL has separate native token-delimiter,
+C-whitespace, name-prefix, and digital-unknown meanings.
+
+## Source inspection and source qualifications
+
+Complete relevant functions read before coding:
+
+- `esl_msafile_psiblast.c`: SetInmap (38), GuessAlphabet (85), Read (184).
+- `esl_msafile_clustal.c`: SetInmap (44), GuessAlphabet (87), Read (188).
+- `esl_msafile_selex.c`: SetInmap (98), GuessAlphabet (140), Read (234), block
+  allocation/growth/destruction, ErrorInBlock (443), read_block (473),
+  first_block (536), other_block, append_block (643).
+- `esl_mem.c`: memnewline (484), memtok (526), memspn (551), memstrcmp (582),
+  memstrpfx, memstrcontains (680).
+- `esl_alphabet.c`: complete RNA/DNA/amino constructors and dsqcat (923),
+  dsqcat_noalloc (961); `esl_msa.c`: SetSeqName (1147).
+- `esl_buffer.c`: GetLine (988), buffer_countline (1755);
+  `esl_msafile.c`: GetLine (1207).
+
+Root clarified these exact source corners in conversation and packet 536's
+additive contract. No diagnostic schema was changed:
+
+- SELEX ErrorInBlock rewinds to the offending content end, before LF/CRLF.
+  `next_byte_offset` reflects that reset; already inspected Events and the
+  record's maximum inspected byte extent remain. The trailing range can overlap
+  inspected Events.
+- First missing SELEX data with unsafe line-minus-one formation, negative
+  ntext, no-sequence allocation, non-ASCII C-ctype use, and a later PSI/Clustal
+  row beyond the native growable array allocation remain unavailable with null
+  native status. They are not native-oracle test inputs.
+- Non-first missing SELEX data retains the actual rpos name extent and receives
+  native gap columns. Internal literal spaces are gap aliases; tabs are errors.
+- Repeated MM overwrites the same block interval. Its last value survives; every
+  source fragment remains. An annotation is committed in native append order,
+  retaining its contribution even when a later sequence in the block fails.
+  A byte limitation in a completely overwritten MM
+  value does not invalidate the surviving value.
+- PSI/Clustal names use the C-visible prefix before NUL. The full original token
+  stays in its Event. A later full token is compared with that C-visible prefix.
+- SELEX annotation text preserves the full copied bytes, including NUL, through
+  reversible text. A surviving NUL/non-ASCII annotation marks only that
+  annotation invalid with `actual=annotation_byte_interpretation`; successfully
+  decoded rows and native status 0 remain. Downstream character-indexed
+  annotation interpretation is still a root-owned unavailable case.
+- Non-ASCII encountered by native C-ctype remains unavailable. A SELEX internal
+  non-ASCII sequence byte preceded/followed by safe ASCII can instead reach the
+  digital validator and has the defined status-7 rejection.
+
+## Authored verification
+
+Exact complete selector: `tests/test_hmmer_alignment_input_blocks.py`.
+`TEST_SELECTORS.txt` lists every authored test function selector. The test file
+covers packet 534 N05, N06, N07, N13 and N14, closed shapes, lossless byte custody,
+exact native gap/alias coordinates, comments, case/order/geometry failures,
+empty populations, NUL distinctions and source-only unsafe cases.
+
+Literal byte strings and `AUTHORED_NATIVE_CASES.json` are authored edge cases,
+not native observations. `FIXTURE_INDEX.json` identifies the unchanged retained
+native emissions and upstream fixtures with their actual hashes. No producer
+was rerun. The authentic cmemit output tests expect the retained 3-row/12-column
+single-block and 2-row/74-column two-block Clustal alignments. Upstream SELEX
+fixtures 1/2 expect 5 rows and 20/40 columns; fixture 3 remains unavailable at
+its first missing-data source corner. Fixture 4 expects 11 rows/31 columns.
+These are test expectations, not this packet's test results.
+
+Performed here: source/contract/fixture reading, stdlib file writes and hashes,
+and `ast.parse` of the owned module and tests. No application imports, pytest,
+compilation, native calls, scientific producers, live execution, adapter changes,
+scoring calculations, or integration were performed by this agent. Root receives
+all files for bounded validation and further repair. A full authored diff is in
+`OWNED_DIFF.patch` (including authored verification files, excluding the
+self-referential generated diff/hash indexes); hashes excluding the
+self-describing hash file are in `OWNED_HASHES.json`.
